  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Icream** (1 other source): Icream was actually the opening song, not the closer as the track listing picture wrongly shows [1]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Icream**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [4]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **mmj2001-03-02.BRYCC** (recommended): source not stated; 9 songs; 54 min; rated 4/5 by 2 [1]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- The show was a benefit for Landy Valdez; a poster announcing it is in an online MMJ live archive [2]\n- Landy Valdez was a Louisville man who died in summer 2000 from an accidental gunshot [3]\n- March 2 was Valdez's birthday, which the reviewer believes is why the show was played that date [3]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **mmj2001-03-02.BRYCC**: taped by Lee Gutterman; transferred by Lee Gutterman; source: Unknown [1]. Also: Transfer chain: MD to CD, then EAC rip to wav, then flac [1]",
